<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose four points to 1,286.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose four points to 1,286.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,286 today from 1,282 on June 18, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1366    12.400	  1357    12.319</p>
<p>   1a   1304  9879.000	  1286  9744.000</p>
<p>   2    1519    21.700	  1514    21.625</p>
<p>   2a   1509 12379.000	  1494 12250.000</p>
<p>   3    1337    12.336	  1336    12.325</p>
<p>   3a   1203  9493.000	  1208  9531.000</p>
